  "description": "meme-id: hurry_up_son_the_owner_is_coming; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two Samoyed dogs, one adult and one puppy, with text overlaid that reads 'hurry up son, the owner is coming.' The scene is benign and humorous, playing on the common trope of pets being anxious or eager to please their owners. The meme's intent is to evoke laughter through anthropomorphism and relatable pet behavior. There is no toxicity present, as it does not target any protected group or promote harmful stereotypes. The humor is derived from the dogs' perceived obedience and the owner's implied authority, which is a lighthearted and non-harmful analogy. The meme is not abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic. It is a harmless, universally relatable joke about pet behavior.",
